Key insights:
1. A string can be reordered to a palindrome if at most 1 character appears an odd number of times
2. After reordering rows, for columns to be palindromes, symmetric rows (from top/bottom) must have identical character multisets
3. This allows ordered rows to satisfy column palindrome constraints

